# Semgrep ignore patterns (gitignore syntax).
# Semgrep already skips .gitignore'd paths (node_modules, dist, vendor, ...).
# We only add tracked paths that Semgrep's parser genuinely cannot read, which
# otherwise surface as warning-level SARIF notifications and make GitHub report
# "Semgrep OSS is reporting errors".

# Kubernetes manifests are Helm templates ({{ .Values.* }}) — not valid
# standalone YAML, so Semgrep's YAML parser fails on every file. This exclusion
# is inherent to Helm templating, not a workaround for a fixable file. Nothing
# else lints them either (yamllint's lint-config does not recurse this deep).
kubernetes/templates/
